Changes made for the Lure TTS (2026), as required by section 4(b) of the license:

- Scope: only the Qwen3-TTS model path, the framework code it links, ggml and the vendored
  libraries it needs are kept. Other model families, the upstream CLI, server, web UI, model
  manager, upstream C API, tests, scripts and documentation were removed, and CMakeLists.txt
  was rewritten for the reduced tree. src/framework/audio/dsp.* lost an unused log-mel
  extractor, and comments throughout src/ and include/ were edited.
- Qwen3-TTS prompt (src/models/qwen3_tts/, include/engine/models/qwen3_tts/): a per-segment
  prompt builder (prompt_segment.cpp) for the icl, xvec, custom_voice and voice_design modes
  in both the non_streaming and streaming layouts, x-vector-only voices, an instruct
  (direction) prefix in every mode, dialect speakers with language auto, NFC-normalized
  tokenization, a prefill recipe dump with mode, layout and trailing rows, an incremental
  attention-mask upload in the talker's cached step, and a 72-frame left context for the
  streaming codec decode.
- Loader (assets.cpp): tensor shape checks against config.json for the 0.6B and 1.7B
  Base, CustomVoice and VoiceDesign checkpoints, a config-and-tokenizer-only metadata path,
  case-insensitive speaker names, and a Turbo hidden size taken from the code predictor.
- Turbo head: grouped code predictor (turbo_head.cpp, turbo_head.h) selected from turbo.json,
  and the converter's support for it (app/gguf/main.cpp, model_specs/qwen3_tts.json).
- New: the Lure TTS C API (include/lure_tts.h, src/lure/), lure_cli with its HTTP
  server (app/lure/), the Python ctypes binding (python/lure_cpp), the prompt conformance
  tool (tools/lure/) and the unit tests (tests/).
- Converter (app/gguf/main.cpp, src/framework/assets/tensor_source.cpp): --hf-dir input and
  symlinked sidecar directories.
- ggml Metal (external/ggml/src/ggml-metal/ggml-metal-device.m): optional lookup of
  precompiled metallibs next to the library.
- CMakePresets.json with portable CPU flags for the GPU presets.

